WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:12.402
Hi! Why do we say I enjoy reading, but I want to read? Today we'll learn about -ing verbs, to plus a verb, and the difference between boring and bored.

2
00:00:12.552 --> 00:00:24.018
Some verbs are followed by an -ing form, called a gerund. For example: enjoy, finish, avoid, keep, mind and practise. I enjoy reading.

3
00:00:24.168 --> 00:00:35.610
Other verbs are followed by to plus a verb, called an infinitive. For example: want, hope, decide, plan, promise and agree. I want to read.

4
00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:44.658
After a preposition, always use the -ing form: She is good at drawing. Wash your hands before eating.

5
00:00:44.808 --> 00:00:51.690
To plus a verb can also show purpose, why someone does something. She went to the shop to buy bread.

6
00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:56.442
He saved money to buy a bicycle. That's why he saved.

7
00:00:56.592 --> 00:01:05.778
Careful with look forward to. Here, to is a preposition, so it's followed by -ing: I look forward to meeting you.

8
00:01:05.928 --> 00:01:14.298
The -ing and -ed forms can be adjectives too. -ing describes the thing that causes a feeling: The film was boring.

9
00:01:14.448 --> 00:01:18.474
-ed describes how a person feels: I was bored.

10
00:01:18.624 --> 00:01:23.274
The news was exciting, so we were excited.

11
00:01:23.424 --> 00:01:29.994
A participle can also join two sentences. The pupils heard the bell. They lined up.

12
00:01:30.144 --> 00:01:37.578
We can write: Hearing the bell, the pupils lined up. The ones who heard the bell are the pupils, right after the comma.

13
00:01:37.728 --> 00:01:43.890
Make sure the subject after the comma is the one doing the -ing action.

14
00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:48.258
Watch out! I am interesting in science is wrong!

15
00:01:48.408 --> 00:01:52.674
This is about how I feel about science, so we need interested.

16
00:01:52.824 --> 00:01:58.794
We use -ing for the thing itself: Science is interesting.

17
00:01:58.944 --> 00:02:08.874
Your turn! She has finished ___ her essay. To write or writing? Pause and think.

18
00:02:09.024 --> 00:02:16.266
The answer is writing, because finish is followed by -ing. Did you get it right?

19
00:02:16.416 --> 00:02:26.514
Another one! We decided ___ the museum. Visiting or to visit? Pause and think.

20
00:02:26.664 --> 00:02:34.098
The answer is to visit, because decide is followed by to plus a verb. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:34.248 --> 00:02:44.610
Last one! The roller coaster ride was ___. Terrified or terrifying? Pause and think.

22
00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:52.410
The answer is terrifying, because it describes the ride that causes the fear. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:52.560 --> 00:03:07.386
Remember: enjoy, finish, avoid and prepositions are followed by -ing. Want, decide and hope take to plus a verb, and to plus a verb can show purpose. -ing describes the thing; -ed describes the feeling.

24
00:03:07.536 --> 00:03:11.850
Tell someone what you enjoy doing most!

